      "summary": "The secret scan can be bypassed by a tracked filename beginning with an option. That leaves a reachable path for credentials in tracked files to pass the workflow.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": ".github/workflows/build.yml",
          "line": 46,
          "message": "A02:2025 — Prevent tracked filenames from being interpreted as cp options; a filename such as `--help` can leave the gitleaks scan directory empty and let committed credentials pass.",
          "confidence": 0.91,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The secret scan passes tracked paths from `git ls-files` to `cp` without an option terminator. GNU cp treats a tracked path beginning with `-` as an option; `--help`, for example, makes cp exit successfully without copying the files. The workflow then runs gitleaks on the empty scan directory.",
            "failureScenario": "A pull request adds a tracked root file named `--help` containing a credential. The copy command exits successfully without staging the tracked files, gitleaks finds nothing, and the workflow passes with the credential committed (OWASP A02:2025)."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
