        "suggestion": 0
      },
      "summary": "The tracked-file secret scan can miss credentials in package-lock.json because gitleaks' default allowlist skips that file, and the source checker allows query parameters on npmjs.org resolution URLs.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": ".github/workflows/build.yml",
          "line": 51,
          "message": "A02:2025 — The default gitleaks allowlist skips package-lock.json, while the source checker permits credential-bearing query parameters on npmjs.org URLs. A committed token in a resolved URL can therefore evade both checks.",
          "confidence": 0.9,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The secret scan runs gitleaks with its default rules over copied tracked files. The test comment at backend/AirlineDemo.Api.Tests/SupplyChainWorkflowTests.cs:370 notes that gitleaks' default allowlist skips package-lock.json. The source checker permits query parameters on npmjs.org resolution URLs.",
            "failureScenario": "If frontend/package-lock.json contains a resolved URL such as https://registry.npmjs.org/pkg.tgz?token=secret, the source checker accepts its host and gitleaks skips the file. CI can pass with the credential committed (OWASP A02:2025)."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
